From: Manolis Nikiforakis <manolis@weatherxm.com>
Subject: [PATCH] sensor: t23/sc2336 selectable readout modes

Add a sensor_mode module parameter with a per-mode timing table:
0 stock 1080p (now up to 32 fps), 1 the 1280x720@60 table from
espressif/esp-video-components, 2-6 experimental centre crops / full-width
strips derived from those tables by reprogramming window and HTS/VTS at the
same 81 MHz PLL, 7 experimental 2x2 bin/skip (SC200AI recipe; corrupt
image on SC2336, kept for research).  Limits measured on a T23N: the ISP
needs >= ~30 lines of vertical blanking.

Also cap exposure at VTS-6 instead of VTS-4: at VTS-4 the SC2336
stretches the frame (1080p30 measured at 33.50 ms instead of 33.33).
---
--- a/common/sensor/t23/sc2336.c	2026-10-30 23:42:22
+++ b/common/sensor/t23/sc2336.c	2026-10-31 01:46:09
@@ -49,6 +49,18 @@
 static int shvflip = 0;
 module_param(shvflip, int, S_IRUGO);
 MODULE_PARM_DESC(shvflip, "Sensor HV Flip Enable interface");
